==============================================================================
(d) BASE CASE: coefficient of g_r(m-1,b) in (*) at m = b+r+1
==============================================================================
  rearranged (*) is  m*g_r(m,b) - (m-1-r-b)*g_r(m-1,b) = 1 + r h_(r-1)(n-m+1,b)
  because  m*[g(m)-g(m-1)] + (1+r+b) g(m-1) = m g(m) - (m-(1+r+b)) g(m-1),
  and m-(1+r+b) = -b + m - r - 1 = m-1-r-b.  Consistent with the ORIGINAL rule
  g_r(m,b)=1/m + (r/m)h_(r-1) + ((m-1-r-b)/m) g_r(m-1,b).
  At m = b+r+1:  coefficient (m-1-r-b) = 0  -> ZERO exactly.

==============================================================================
(c) CONTRACTION COEFFICIENT FOR THE RESIDUAL
==============================================================================
  Residual terms in the substitution:  m[R(m)-R(m-1)] + (1+r+b) R(m-1)
                                     = m R(m) - (m-1-r-b) R(m-1).
  So  R(m) = ((m-1-r-b)/m) R(m-1) + (1/m)[ r eps^h_(r-1) - Delta_r ],
  and ((m-1-r-b)/m) is IDENTICAL to g_r's own recursion's contraction
  coefficient -- same operator, hence the same telescoping structure.

